@copilot Please replace the explicit container-test class list with source-file discovery in this PR.

Move all ten container-test classes into `io.opentelemetry.instrumentation.jmx.rules.containers`, and move the `KafkaContainer` helper into that package too. Keep the existing test source set, shared base class, verifier, and assertions. Update package declarations and imports as needed.

Replace the hard-coded list with this discovery block:

```kotlin
val containerTestPackage =
  "io.opentelemetry.instrumentation.jmx.rules.containers"

val containerTestClasses = fileTree("src/test/java") {
  include("${containerTestPackage.replace('.', '/')}/*Test.java")
}.files
  .map { "$containerTestPackage.${it.nameWithoutExtension}" }
  .sorted()

require(containerTestClasses.isNotEmpty()) {
  "No JMX container test classes found"
}
```

Keep the existing per-class task names, exact class filters, default `test` exclusions, classpath, `testcontainersBuildService` usage, shared artifact and registry inputs, JVM argument providers, standard timeouts, and `check` dependencies. Adding a new `*Test.java` directly in the container package should automatically register its task and exclude it from the default task. Helpers such as `KafkaContainer.java` must not be selected.

Verify discovery works before compilation on a clean checkout and that all ten existing classes remain covered exactly once. Do not add annotation scanning, a new source set, or CI partitioning changes. Update the PR description if its package or discovery explanation becomes stale.
